<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n83220" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πῑνο-τήρης</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ου</span>,
			ὁ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τηρέω</span>)
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>pinna-guard, a small
			crab</i> that lives in the pinna's shell, said to give warning of
			approaching danger, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				547b28
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Chrysipp.Stoic.
				2.207
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.980b
			</span></i>; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πινυφύλαξ</span>.
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> metaph., of a
			diminutive person, 'baby-crab', <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>V.</u>
				1510
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ π. τοῦδε μάντεως
			χορός</span> (prob. for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χοροῦ</span>),
			posted to give warning, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				113
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
